     kkyyuuaa hheellpp — Shows usage information

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     kkyyuuaa hheellpp [_c_o_m_m_a_n_d]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The kkyyuuaa hheellpp command provides interactive help on all supported commands
     and options.  If, for some reason, you happen to spot a discrepancy in
     the output of this command and this document, the command is the authori‐
     tative source of information.

     If no arguments are provided, the command prints the list of common op‐
     tions and the list of supported subcommands.

     If the _c_o_m_m_a_n_d argument is provided to, this single argument is the name
     of a valid subcommand.  In that case, kkyyuuaa hheellpp prints a textual descrip‐
     tion of the command, the list of common options and the list of subcom‐
     mand-specific options.

EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS
     The kkyyuuaa hheellpp command always returns 0.

     Additional exit codes may be returned as described in kyua(1).

